From 7fe6def35a91cdb48ffcd405a9c46b883b3e7224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 04:48:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix memory leak: replace Manager().Queue() with
 multiprocessing.Queue

multiprocessing.Manager().Queue() spawns a background Manager subprocess
that was never explicitly shut down, causing a resource leak. Replace it
with a plain multiprocessing.Queue() which requires no subprocess.

Additional cleanup to support this change:
- Add sentinel value (None) shutdown pattern for the queue reader thread
- Replace sys.exit() calls in check_finished() with threading.Event
  signaling, allowing the main thread to coordinate shutdown properly
- Add wait() and shutdown() methods to EventHandler for clean lifecycle
- Add _close_queue() to release queue resources
- In exitmap.py: use try/finally to ensure controller.close() is called
  and handler.shutdown() runs after iter_exit_relays() completes

The sys.exit() calls in check_finished() were problematic because they
could terminate the process from a background thread, bypassing cleanup.
The new approach signals completion via an Event and lets the main thread
orchestrate orderly shutdown.

Co-authored-by: 1aeo <1aeo@users.noreply.github.com>
